course: dictionary
lesson: 12200
title: Conform: fit in, or meet the rule
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To conform means to do what most people do, or what you are expected to do. It can also mean to obey a rule or meet a standard. «All the toys must conform to safety rules.» The toys follow the rules, so they meet them.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Jess wanted to be different, so she did not conform to the uniform rules.» Did not conform is the opposite of following the rules, so conform means to follow them. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence: "Jess did not follow the uniform rules" still makes sense.
explain: Conform can also mean to fit a shape. «The new lid will conform to the shape of the jar.» Conform is often followed by "to" or "with", as in conform to a rule or conform with a plan.
fact: Conform means to behave the way most people do, or the way you are expected to.
fact: «Conform to» a rule or standard means to obey it or meet it.
fact: «Conform» can also mean to fit a shape exactly.
fact: Safety labels such as CE or UKCA show that a product meets safety standards.
fact: A character who refuses to conform chooses to stand out and be different.
exercise: «Every pupil must conform to the school uniform rules.» What does conform mean here? | *Obey | Paint | Lose | Break
exercise: «The lid will conform to the shape of the jar.» What does conform mean here? | *Fit the shape | Melt away | Shout loudly | Break into pieces
exercise: In the story, Ella refuses to conform. What does this suggest? | She is very tired | She always does exactly what everyone else does | *She chooses to stand out and be different | She is afraid of the dark
test: «Check that the toy conforms to safety standards.» What does conforms mean here? | *Meets | Hides from | Sings to | Breaks
test: Which phrase means to follow a plan? | To invent | To lose | To ignore | *To conform with
exam: «Sam did not conform, so he stood out in the photo.» What does conform mean in this sentence? | Lose his way | Shout loudly | Run away | *Behave the way others do
